# Example deny list for tools/sync-skills.sh
#
# Copy to ~/.thiri/skills-deny.txt (or set DENY_FILE=/path/to/list) and replace these
# with your own. The real list is deliberately not in this repo: the patterns name the
# exact symbols and phrases worth protecting, so a public copy of the list would leak
# the thing the gate exists to keep back.
#
# Format: <regex>@@<why>
#   - one rule per line; '#' comments and blank lines are ignored
#   - the regex is passed to `grep -rIinE`, so it may contain alternations
#   - the '@@' delimiter exists because '|' cannot: the patterns contain '|' themselves,
#     and splitting on it silently truncated them into invalid regex
#   - <why> is printed when a rule fires, so write it for the person who has to act
#
# Good rules name a thing that is checkable, not a vibe. "Do not leak the algorithm" is
# not a rule; the header name the algorithm lives in is.

MySecretClass@@internal class name
my_internal_flag@@internal mode name
the special sauce@@internal doctrine
private-repo-name@@private repository name
[Pp]assword[[:space:]]*[:=][[:space:]]*[^ <$]@@a literal credential
